CAT = "nzfkPreop"; SEG = "PRE"
# Pre-operation inspection, consumables, start-up, fault reporting (NZQA 40735 outcomes 1 and 2).
Q = [
('Which four areas does skill standard 40735 list for a pre-operation inspection?',
 'Consumables, leaks, damage, function', ['Paint, seat, mirrors, lights, cab', 'Fuel, radio, horn, cab, keys', 'Tyres, load, pallets, racking'],
 "40735's indicative content lists consumables, leaks, damage and operational safety as the pre-operation inspection."),
('Why is the pre-operation inspection done before the forklift moves?',
 'To catch faults before use', ['To warm the hydraulic oil', "To log the operator's hours", 'To charge the battery fully'],
 'Skill standard 40735 sets the pre-operation inspection before start-up, so leaks, damage and failed controls are found before the truck is used.'),
('Which of these does skill standard 40735 class as a consumable?',
 'Hydraulic fluid', ['Load backrest', 'Overhead guard', 'Mast rails'],
 '40735 defines consumables as items such as tyres, hydraulic fluids, fuel, oils, coolant, battery charge state and water level.'),
("Why are tyres counted among a forklift's consumables?",
 'They wear out with use', ['They hold the counterweight', 'They set the lift height', 'They store hydraulic oil'],
 'Tyres wear with use, so 40735 lists them with fluids and fuel as consumables to check and replace.'),
('During the pre-start check, a pool of oil sits under the mast. What should happen?',
 'Have it checked before use', ['Wipe it up and drive on', 'Use it until the shift ends', 'Top up the fluid and carry on'],
 "A leak is a defect: report it under the site's fault reporting procedure and do not use the truck until it is assessed. Topping up hides the problem."),
("A fork's positioning lock is missing, so the fork slides on the carriage. What should happen?",
 'Tag the truck out of use', ['Use it for light loads only', 'Wedge the fork with timber', 'Lift only to knee height'],
 "Missing or damaged fork positioning locks are a standard pre-shift check item. A sliding fork can drop the load; the truck stays out of use until repaired."),
("Which check is part of 'operational safety' before use?",
 'Brakes and steering work', ['Stock levels in racking', 'Colour of the pallets', 'Volume of the cab radio'],
 'Before use the operator confirms the brakes, steering, lift, tilt and warning devices work, so the truck can be stopped and controlled.'),
('Before starting, an operator finds the horn does not work. What is right?',
 'Keep it parked until fixed', ['Use it and shout at corners', 'Use it in quiet areas only', 'Log it and fix it next week'],
 'The horn is a warning device that is part of the pre-shift check. A failed safety device is a fault to report before the truck is used.'),
("Which item is part of skill standard 40735's start-up procedure?",
 'Seatbelt and restraints', ['Raising the forks fully', 'Tuning the cab radio', 'Tilting the mast forward'],
 "40735's start-up content is operator restraints (seatbelts), three points of contact and the correct driving position."),
("What does 'three points of contact' mean when getting on a forklift?",
 'Three of four limbs on', ['Seat, steering and pedal', 'Both feet on the step only', 'One hand on the mast'],
 'Keeping three of your four limbs on the truck when mounting or dismounting stops slips and falls. 40735 lists it for start-up and shut-down.'),
('Why must the operator be in the correct driving position before moving?',
 'To reach every control', ['To make the horn louder', 'To keep the battery cool', 'To lower the mast faster'],
 '40735 lists the correct driving position in start-up: seated, restrained and able to reach the controls without leaning outside the truck.'),
("Which item about the operator is part of 40735's environment check?",
 'Fit to operate it', ['Holds a class 2 licence', 'Owns their own boots', 'Belongs to a union'],
 "40735's environment check includes human safety factors and whether the operator is fit to operate the forklift."),
('A worker took a medicine that says it may cause drowsiness. What should they do before driving a forklift?',
 'Stand down; tell the supervisor', ['Drive slowly for the shift', 'Drink coffee and carry on', 'Drive only in the yard'],
 "Being fit to operate is part of the pre-start check. A worker must take reasonable care for their own and others' safety under section 45."),
('What does skill standard 40735 expect of fault reporting?',
 "The site's reporting procedure", ['Repairing the fault yourself', 'Telling a friend on shift', 'Chalking it on the truck'],
 "40735 asks operators to describe fault reporting procedures: report faults through the site's procedure so the truck is assessed and repaired by someone competent."),
('A gas forklift smells strongly of LPG at start-up. What first?',
 'Shut off; no ignition near', ['Start it to clear the gas', 'Drive it outside quickly', 'Use a lighter to look'],
 'LPG is heavier than air and can collect in low areas. Shut the gas off, keep ignition sources away and report it.'),
('An LPG forklift will be left overnight. What should be done with its gas supply?',
 'Turn it off at the cylinder', ['Leave it on for a quick start', 'Disconnect the battery only', 'Open the valve slightly'],
 "On LPG trucks, turn the gas supply off at the cylinder when the truck is left for some time, such as overnight, so a leak cannot build up gas."),
('Why must LPG not be changed near pits or drains?',
 'LPG is heavier than air', ['LPG is lighter than air', 'Drains spark when wet', 'Pits cool the cylinder'],
 'LPG sinks and can gather in low, unventilated places where it may ignite.'),
('What does battery charging release that can explode?',
 'Hydrogen gas', ['Carbon monoxide', 'Nitrogen gas', 'Oxygen-free air'],
 "Charging lead-acid batteries, including 'maintenance free' ones, gives off explosive hydrogen. Charge in a ventilated area with no ignition sources."),
('Which is the right place to charge a forklift battery?',
 'Ventilated, no ignition', ['Sealed room to keep it warm', 'Beside the LPG cage', 'Next to the welding bay'],
 'Battery charging gives off hydrogen, so use a designated, well-ventilated area where smoking, naked flames and other ignition sources are banned.'),
('Who should change a forklift battery between shifts?',
 'Someone trained to do it', ['Whoever finishes first', 'Any visitor on site', 'The first driver in'],
 'Battery changing needs a safe system of work and a person with suitable training and instruction, because batteries are heavy and acid can splash.'),
('When should battery water levels be topped up?',
 'As the maker specifies', ['Before every single lift', 'Only once the truck stops', 'Never on any battery'],
 'Topping-up intervals are set by the battery maker, and levels should be checked after charging and topped up as specified.'),
('Where should a diesel forklift be refuelled?',
 'Outside with the engine off', ['Inside with the engine running', 'Beside an open drain', 'In a closed loading bay'],
 'Refuel outside with the engine switched off, no smoking, and away from places where spilled fuel vapour could gather.'),
('Why does a forklift engine running indoors need ventilation?',
 'Exhaust such as carbon monoxide', ['Too much oxygen builds up', 'The horn needs fresh air', 'Hydraulic fluid evaporates'],
 'Internal combustion trucks give off exhaust fumes including carbon monoxide, so buildings need adequate ventilation.'),
('During the pre-start, an operator finds a weeping hydraulic hose. Which part of the job is theirs?',
 'Logging it for a fitter', ['Replacing the hose themself', 'Tightening it and driving on', 'Wrapping it with tape'],
 "Operators check and report; repairs are done by a competent, authorised person to the manufacturer's specifications. 40735 asks operators to describe fault reporting procedures."),
('A seatbelt is frayed. What is the right action?',
 'Tag it out until replaced', ['Tie a knot to shorten it', 'Drive without fastening it', 'Use it only for short trips'],
 'The restraint is a safety device that protects the operator in a tipover. A damaged one is a fault to report before use.'),
('What does checking the hydraulic oil level with the forks lowered achieve?',
 'An accurate fluid reading', ['Faster lifting all shift', 'A cooler battery', 'Longer tyre life'],
 'Fluid levels are read with the forks in the parked, lowered position so the oil is back in the tank and the reading is correct.'),
('Why should tyre pressures on pneumatic tyres be checked?',
 'Low pressure reduces stability', ['High pressure saves battery', 'Low pressure raises lift height', 'It stops the horn sticking'],
 "An under-inflated tyre lets the truck lean, reducing stability and affecting steering and braking. Keep pressures at the maker's figure."),
('A forklift has no daily check record for the shift. What should the next operator do?',
 'Complete the check before use', ["Assume yesterday's check holds", 'Drive and check later', 'Ask a driver to vouch for it'],
 "Each shift's operator does the pre-operation inspection before use; a previous check does not cover faults that arose since."),
]
